# Scope

User requested continued verification followed by local and nightly deployment.
Implementation commit 9d1666f contains the bounded retry regressions and
independent production TUI factory callback fix; publication and installed
verification are recorded below.
No live history, queue, cursor, replay, quarantine or fleet stop is authorized.

# Gates

Preliminary tests found concrete issues (shared allowance across outer loops,
unreadable HTTPError body, malformed field types); all three were corrected
and covered by final regressions. Historical loopback runs bind their own
recorded source hashes, not final source.
Existing generic overload policy may retry ambiguous5xx; the new explicit
no-output branch is not an unconditional prohibition on pre-existing overload
retry. Final exact-file suite, loopback, lint and package checks passed.

# Prior release

0f5014d is published/installed successfully; its release evidence is separate
at ../runtime-recovery/. Walkie restart is confirmed but fresh-input end-to-end
delivery remains held by incomplete ownership history. This release must not
claim to repair those live records.

# Final source verification

Final retry source hashes:
- ciel_runtime_support/router_http.py: 2d1cd4f0306a096ef4ef4e56636af5699eddf9dc28091428fa79b7179a4d938d
- tests/test_codex_no_output_http_retry.py: 2067e70996c26e29947260044008ce84613f03a63be405467b01b52b6405d418
The exact isolated integrated suite ran421 tests, zero failures/errors,54 skips.
The retry/TUI focused sources and related modules were included. TUI-only
verification ran12 tests successfully. Real owned loopback retry acceptance
passed all seven final-source cases, including bounded explicit no-output retry,
body preservation, malformed/incomplete error-body rejection, and no replay
after an opened-stream failure. The accepted TUI browser fixture displayed:
`observation stream live | session delivery admission_blocked | known queued 1 |
wake_history_incomplete line 2`; screenshot `evidence/source-tui-held.png`.
Fixture source bytes were unchanged and owned listeners closed.
Repository ruff, py_compile, documentation metadata, OKF strict projections,
diff check and npm pack dry-run passed. Existing overload retry remains a
separate policy and may retry ambiguous5xx; this release does not claim to
remove that behavior.

